+### Bounded first-wait listener contracts (work in progress)
+
+Feedback acceptance is currently red at the reached
+`insightEmailExecutionListener.processMailTask(execution, "start")` on
+`submitter-notification`. Its archive uses a parallel gateway, whose exits ignore
+conditions in both legacy Activiti and Flowable. Although the archive sets
+`skipEmails=true`, that variable does not suppress the native mail branch.
+The real notification listener and native-mail configuration/transport path must
+be implemented before Feedback's first wait can persist. No placeholder or
+skip-mail behavior has been added, and no customer parity row has been promoted.
+
+`insightLdapListener.setLdapProcessVariables(task)` supports MDCR's
+`originate-mdcr` task only. It resolves the persisted Insight user by the
+JWT/legacy authenticated principal's ID, requires an active user and matching
+username/initiator, and maps `userName`, `firstName`, `lastName`, and `email` to
+`originator_id`, `originator_first_name`, `originator_last_name`, and
+`originator_email`. These mappings are established by legacy
+`insight-app/acm/config-insight-acm-mapping.json` at snapshot `525716d6c` and the
+current ACM-synchronized UserEntity. Department, title, and phone have no
+established current entity mapping and are deliberately outside the supported
+subset; no customer values are fabricated. The archive's literal `$INITIATOR`
+assignee is resolved to the trusted username. Missing/mismatched/inactive
+identity refuses the command, including any reporting-ID allocation and earlier
+name changes. The adapter has no mutable delegate fields or remote LDAP calls.
+
+Feedback first reaches `insightJsonUtilListener.extractDisplayTextToColumn`.
+It copies the reference table, selects displayText with hyperlink fallback (or a
+literal string), and persists the JSON string once all rows validate. An absent
+table preserves the source behavior; malformed JSON/non-object rows fail before
+writes. The reached `activiti_flowConditionsBean.exists` gateway operation
+recognizes Boolean false as present; dotted-variable paths are unsupported.
+
+Feedback's `local-review-feedback` task uses a persisted exact-key contract:
+
+- A non-deleted `ReferenceDataLookup` of type `workflow-task-routing`, key
+  `SafranFeedbackWorkflow/local-review-feedback`, contains textual metadata
+  `processKey`, `taskKey`, `lookupVariable`, `lookupType`, and `taskName`.
+- Both process/task keys must match the deployed task. The supported lookup
+  variable is `submitting_site`; its nonblank String value selects an exact
+  key from the configured lookupType, distinct from `workflow-task-routing`.
+- That non-deleted lookup row contains `candidateGroup`, the stable name of an
+  active functional Insight group. Group resolution is separate from lookup.
+  The resolved numeric Insight group ID replaces the archive candidate IDs,
